-- title:
--   Exactness of the Hopf-kernel tower: Γᵥ=Γᵥ₊₁[p^v]
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative local domain that is a principal ideal ring, let $p$ and $i_0$ be natural numbers, and let $B_w$ ($w\in\mathbb N$) be commutative rings carrying Hopf $R$-algebra structures with cocommutative comultiplication and finite free underlying $R$-modules. Suppose given bialgebra maps $t_w\colon B_{w+1}\to B_w$, each surjective, and bialgebra maps $m_w\colon B_w\to B_{w+1}$ such that $m_w\circ t_w$ is the $p$-th convolution power $[p]^*$ of the identity on $B_{w+1}$ and $t_w\circ m_w$ is $[p]^*$ on $B_w$, and suppose that for every $w\ge i_0$ the map $m_{w+1}$ carries the Hopf kernel of $t_w$ (the subalgebra of $a\in B_{w+1}$ with $(\mathrm{id}\otimes t_w)\Delta(a)=a\otimes 1$) bijectively onto the Hopf kernel of $t_{w+1}$ inside $B_{w+2}$. Write $T_{v+1}=t_{i_0}\circ\cdots\circ t_{i_0+v}$ for the iterated transition $B_{i_0+v+1}\to B_{i_0}$. Then for every $v$ and every $x$ in the Hopf kernel of $T_{v+1}$ one has $t_{i_0+v}(x)=0$ if and only if $x$ lies in the ideal of $B_{i_0+v+1}$ generated by the image under the algebra endomorphism $[p^v]^*$ of the intersection of that Hopf kernel with the augmentation ideal (the kernel of the counit).
--
--   This is the exactness step in Tate's proof that the tower of quotients $\Gamma_v=E_{i_0+v}/E_{i_0}$ is $p$-divisible: in Hopf-algebraic form, the level $\Gamma_v$ is exactly the $p^v$-torsion of $\Gamma_{v+1}$, the ideal description of the kernel coming from the identification of the kernel of a surjection of finite free Hopf algebras with the ideal generated by the augmentation ideal of its Hopf kernel. It is used in the construction of the $p$-divisible group attached to the stabilised tower, [`PDivisibleGroup.Tower.exists_tower_hopfKer_transitionLE_of_bijOn_hopfKer`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.Tower.exists_tower_hopfKer_transitionLE_of_bijOn_hopfKer).
